  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Providing Technical and Capacity Building Support to the Government of Sudan and Local Communities on Disaster Risk Reduction and Emergency Preparedness - Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan currently faces various challenges in managing man-made and disasters related to various natural hazards due to a combination of political and socio-economic instability and exacerbated by an extreme biophysical vulnerability. Through this project, IOM aims to contribute to minimizing the adverse impacts of disasters such as floods and droughts especially among the most vulnerable communities in Sudan by developing the capacities of government ministries in the management of storage facilities and emergency relief supplies for preparedness and response in the country whilst contributing to development of local capacities through community-based solutions and risk reduction mechanisms.</narrative>
  </description>
